{"_doc": "Per-region metadata for the misfits atlas map: which name(s) label each lod0 region, a faction family for colouring, and 2290-era political standing/scale. Names are resolved by point-in-polygon: each seed in region-labels.json is tested against every region in atlas-regions.lod0.topojson, and the containing region's id is the key below. `family` is set only when one of a region's resolved names appears in faction-families.json's steelFamily list \u2014 it is a lookup against recorded evidence, never an inference, so most regions omit it. `standing`/`scale` are set only when the region's id appears in a 2290-territories.json territory's mainRegions \u2014 again omitted, not guessed, when no territory claims the region. `nameSource` says which sheet each name was read off, keyed into the top-level `sources` block, so the 2026-08-14 naming ruling - better-registered source wins, ties to the earlier import, neither registered means neither is drawn - can be applied and checked mechanically instead of by hand. `primaryRuledBy` marks a drawn name chosen by an owner ruling rather than by that comparison. Every residual in `sources` is copied from SOURCE-REGISTER.json at build time and none is written by hand. `subDetail` lists the names this region catches that are NOT its primary, each with the class that says why - a district the artwork drew inside this outline, or an alias, duplicate transcription, typo, fragment or a name an owner ruling displaced. Only `draw: true` entries are drawn, as POINTS INSIDE the host by tools/build-subregion-detail.mjs; no outline is edited and no boundary is claimed. A suppressed name is still shipped, in names[] and here, because a loser is subordinated and never removed. Regenerate with docs/changes/map-timeline/trace/build_region_meta.py.","sources": {"north-america-2290-factions.png": {"kind": "sheet","registered": false,"residualKm": null,"residualWorstKm": null,"residualStat": null,"importedOn": "2026-07-26","creator": "u/King_Kestrel","permits": "NAMES AND CONTAINMENT ONLY. Unchanged by the 2026-08-07 refit, which improved the model without moving the permission: not boundaries, and not point sites."},"north-america-political.png": {"kind": "sheet","registered": true,"residualKm": 68.2,"residualWorstKm": 122.7,"residualStat": "RMS over the 13 control points, NOT a median. Recorded explicitly because the register's other rows quote medians and comparing the two as though they were the same statistic is a mistake this repository has already flagged (../era-assemblage-state-2026-08-14.md section 3d).","importedOn": "2026-07-25","creator": null,"permits": "NAMES AND CONTAINMENT ONLY, at continental zoom - the 25-100 km row of the source-map-intake Step 3 table. NOT permitted: any point placement a reader could check, and not boundaries."},"region-meta-authored.json": {"kind": "decision","authority": "owner-ruling","registered": false,"residualKm": null,"permits": "whatever the recorded ruling says. An owner ruling is not a measurement and does not compete with one; it settles the case the measurement was going to be used to decide.","note": "Not a sheet and deliberately absent from SOURCE-REGISTER.json. Every record in it carries its own rationale."}},"regions": {"0": {"names": ["Greenland"],"primary": "Greenland","nameSource": {"Greenland": "north-america-political.png"}},"1": {"names": ["Albion and Newfoundland"],"primary": "Albion and Newfoundland","nameSource": {"Albion and Newfoundland": "north-america-political.png"}},"2": {"names": ["Alberta-Saskatchewan Confederation","Montana","Alberta-Saskatchewan","Blackfeet","Jasper","Montana BOS","Nahanni","Colville-Spokane","Kingdom of Olympia","Snake River Republic","Empire of the Khans","Mormonic Clergical Commonwealth","Montana BoS Chapter"],"primary": "Alberta-Saskatchewan Confederation","family": "brotherhood","standing": "sovereign","scale": "district","via": ["Montana BoS Chapter"],"subDetail": [{"name": "Montana","draw": true,"class